before:
```typescript
type Address = { street: string; town: string };
type AddressField = keyof Address;
function readAddress(address: Address, field: AddressField): string {
  return address[field];
}
console.log(readAddress({ street: "Oak Road", town: "Vale" }, "town"));
```
This prints Vale. readAddress takes an Address and an allowed field name, then returns that property. address[field] is runtime bracket access: it uses the value held by field. In contrast, keyof Address describes the allowed names during checking. console.log displays the returned string.

